e-fc94-5328-b3c9-02640b829131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-16198/selection/2c249c8c0ce7c2be017589216f13982a07cce2607e76f6d923584afffacf1a71" :answer-field/choices ["q-16198/selection/825f82701a8088534b084d0e25a0e4c40e50be9a2891ad7378bcf8d077ff02c5" "q-16198/selection/2c249c8c0ce7c2be017589216f13982a07cce2607e76f6d923584afffacf1a71" "q-16198/selection/24990ba80031d5c30ed4c4d0ef0fdf5521f0b52bd494f132690e77428cffb842" "q-16198/selection/aabd2963677251543bbdd5fbd50dd3e01f94f4417fff62bcae4d96c797b3d595" "q-16198/selection/3f70c447004284ce848263985b20c8c49de8a38af0b1fcb9a2bd0b27f65fca0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-16198" :question/id #uuid "70933ef2-8feb-5ff8-b2e4-bedd76dd6bf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-16198" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi \n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-7$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-7$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/assets/debf9475589e7e242df986d1fffb8a97834d6ce550279fc82b0428001b661eaa.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-16198/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16198"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773/selection/c3ec8e62eb3981e4571e6648bfa30618dc0c256e1a502c3067e9c1433972e8ad" :answer/id #uuid "85dd432d-2b85-50fa-a03c-e3549ff229b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773/selection/2314c7655c1c9edc52c08f6cce774df039327926c375e132c9901941963cdd77" :answer/id #uuid "4225080f-f339-5b6d-9f17-95c386185b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773/selection/12efa6b56d580b6ea2dc3fc6ee897c290b21a321d0d98ffc7678ad996193d796" :answer/id #uuid "0efe3651-520d-5470-bd30-82285ca8df52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773/selection/6b8211504f4b340a02f6d3d1206a4e91ae2c27016482a607b79b593b4dbc48bc" :answer/id #uuid "236ce462-6b1e-594b-9a2b-c48888cc132d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773/selection/cbd5552742c5f11ffc3643f3e01f40005011135c07b5bdd82ba95edcf3c6e48b" :answer/id #uuid "5986db54-acb9-514a-af17-5e48d8a6f92e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ee01a6-098b-5d46-91df-c9131ccd83f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123773/selection/cbd5552742c5f11ffc3643f3e01f40005011135c07b5bdd82ba95edcf3c6e48b" :answer-field/choices ["q-123773/selection/c3ec8e62eb3981e4571e6648bfa30618dc0c256e1a502c3067e9c1433972e8ad" "q-123773/selection/2314c7655c1c9edc52c08f6cce774df039327926c375e132c9901941963cdd77" "q-123773/selection/12efa6b56d580b6ea2dc3fc6ee897c290b21a321d0d98ffc7678ad996193d796" "q-123773/selection/6b8211504f4b340a02f6d3d1206a4e91ae2c27016482a607b79b593b4dbc48bc" "q-123773/selection/cbd5552742c5f11ffc3643f3e01f40005011135c07b5bdd82ba95edcf3c6e48b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123773" :question/id #uuid "42535d46-cb00-5afc-82ab-e62c0ea06521" :question/math-academy-id "q-123773" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }\\ge -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -1 \\\\ -1 & \\le -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1-1 & \\le 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1+1 \\\\ 0 & \\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+2 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\le 1+2 \\\\ 1 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123773/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123773"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-1/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer/id #uuid "c9e34dba-6df9-5555-903f-97eb3da427b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "935309e2-1d8b-5d0b-9910-0c3b89a84ea0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326304/field-1/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-326304/field-1/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9748b3ab-2088-5dba-a49d-2e58b8f44d69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a3520c1-4593-5c9f-bceb-5e6e6b1fe671" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326304/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-326304/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-3/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer/id #uuid "23e8fc38-c87a-543b-9fcb-b804965ed003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f92bc1e-818c-5856-a65b-3d8fc1ed0aac" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326304/field-3/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-326304/field-3/b785f042bcb1e3ac9f1c15e72aea8c54b522212617bb84e48c5ba505bb17b3ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0a3bc4e1-6e8d-5c3c-b9b9-7a5a3317106f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc32d3c-367a-5cb0-8eb5-ec45bbd858c5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326304/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-326304/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326304" :question/id #uuid "7d27dc41-abce-5a21-8f11-4131f79addb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-326304" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4t-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2}+3,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t+4)+4 \\\\  & =-(t-2)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-(t-2)^{2}+4\\le 4,$ we conclude that the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that ${t}^{2}+3\\ge 3.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-326304/field-1" "q-326304/field-2" "q-326304/field-3" "q-326304/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} 